== Texture Mods

#mod-entry(
  name: "MELLO",
  url: "https://www.nexusmods.com/masseffectlegendaryedition/mods/1500",
  game: "LE1",
  version: "v1.0",
  last-checked: "2025-11",
  deps: (),
  impact: [Mass Effect 1 Legendary Lighting Overhaul. Restores dynamic lighting lost in the LE update, aiming to produce the best of both worlds---the updated engine's bells and whistles with the cinematic look of the original. Includes customizable post-processing options.],
  notes: none,
)

#mod-entry(
  name: "LEUITM",
  url: "https://www.nexusmods.com/masseffectlegendaryedition/mods/1825",
  game: "LE1",
  version: "v1.0",
  last-checked: "2026-07",
  deps: ("ME3Tweaks Mod Manager",),
  impact: [Lore-friendly HD texture pack for Mass Effect 1 that fixes many vanilla texture-level bugs. Hand-crafted replacements for character faces, armor, environments, and props. Includes LE-specific fixes for upscaling artifacts, UV mapping issues, unaligned teeth, specular/normal map miss-mapping, Asari color correction, and environmental enhancements. Designed to complement MELLO but works independently.],
  notes: [Install AFTER all content mods and DLC mods. Designed to complement MELLO. Install via ME3Tweaks Mod Manager texture tools.],
)

#mod-entry(
  name: "LEDs ON LE1",
  url: "https://www.nexusmods.com/masseffectlegendaryedition/mods/589",
  game: "LE1",
  version: "v3",
  last-checked: "2026-07",
  deps: (),
  impact: [Turns on the armor LEDs that were disabled in the Legendary Edition across most suits in Mass Effect 1. Also tweaks Wrex's vanilla outfit. Simple visual enhancement that restores a missing detail from the original game.],
  notes: [Requires Mass Effect Modder (MEM) to install, not ME3Tweaks Mod Manager. Always install texture mods AFTER content mods.],
)

#mod-entry(
  name: "Zeb's Eye Re-Textures",
  url: "https://www.nexusmods.com/masseffectlegendaryedition/mods/585",
  game: "Launcher",
  version: "v1.0",
  last-checked: "2026-07",
  deps: (),
  impact: [Updated eye textures for human and asari characters across all three Legendary Edition games. Replaces diffuse and normal textures with cleaner, more neutral versions that have less busy detail and a more concave normal map for iris depth. Gives females a smaller pupil in LE1. Compatible with renegade scarring.],
  notes: [Applies to LE1, LE2, and LE3. Requires Mass Effect Modder (MEM) to install. Always install texture mods AFTER content mods. Overwrites any other eye texture mods.],
)

#mod-entry(
  name: "A Lot Of Textures (ALOT) -- LE1",
  url: "https://www.nexusmods.com/masseffectlegendaryedition/mods/363",
  game: "LE1",
  version: "v2021.1.0",
  last-checked: "2026-07",
  deps: (),
  impact: [Massive vanilla-friendly graphical overhaul for Mass Effect 1. Combines hand-crafted texture replacements from the original OT ALOT project (endorsed by BioWare as a key inspiration behind the LE) with a vastly improved Improved Static Lighting (ISL) component. ISL runs ~40,000 light and shadow maps through neural network-based denoising, antialiasing, and upscaling to eliminate blocky shadows and lighting artifacts. Fixes the most glaring upscaling issues in LE with textures for the Presidium sky, text holograms, Legion, Tali, EDI, Garrus, Liara, and more.],
  notes: [Separate download files for LE1, LE2, and LE3 on the same mod page. Two installation methods: MEM (Mass Effect Modder) replaces all matching textures globally and must be installed AFTER all content mods; M3TO (ME3Tweaks Mod Manager Texture Override) replaces at runtime by asset name, can be toggled on/off, and should be installed BEFORE any .mem mods. M3TO is faster and more flexible. Always install texture mods AFTER content mods.],
)

=== Recommended Load Order

Install texture mods in the following order using Mass Effect Modder (MEM). Later mods overwrite earlier ones, so install higher-priority mods last:

#callout("info", [
  + ALOT
  + ALOT ISL
  + 4k Upscaled Armor and Cloth Textures
  + LEUITM
  + Primitives
  + 4k Enhanced Textures MEM
  + Complexion
  + Paramour
  + LEDs ON LE1
  + Zeb's Eye Re-Textures
])
